# UI kit (stack)

- Reach for the project's UI-kit components and hooks first; don't reinvent what the kit provides. Override via the kit's style props / `classNames` API, not by fighting kit internals (see `stack/css`).
- Style variants via `class-variance-authority` routed through the project's `cn` helper; don't scatter raw `clsx` calls (see `stack/css`).
- Forms: kit inputs wired to React Hook Form; wire `label`/`error` props — don't strip them for layout. Form driver is React Hook Form (see `stack/react`); schemas are Zod (see `stack/api`).
- Don't break the kit's a11y when overriding: keep `role`, `aria-*`, and keyboard handlers intact (see `stack/accessibility`).
